{
  "about": "S-onboarding - the frame states and the undrawn states of the Onboarding questionnaire (/onboarding, URL only: nothing links here, check-nav lists it as no-inbound-by-design). All three frames are drawn for a MEMBER (five tabs, Kezdőlap lit, frame-1 the returning member with the knee limitation and the note 'Térdsérülés után óvatosan a mély guggolásokkal.'). That is user@ (M): its recording holds exactly that note, the knee limitation, Izomtömeg, Haladó and 70 minutes. M's saved step is 0, so the frames are reached on M's recording with edits of /profile/step (and frame-3 its refused POST). The freeze's account C (coach, six tabs, no limitation) stays as the extra state onboarding-step5-coach. Nothing is written live: every PATCH / POST is a fixture answer (PATCH /onboarding 200 {} as in S-settings settings-2; a refusal in the error envelope). Capture limits: the tool cannot hold a request open, so 'saving' (the 700 ms debounce + request) and 'finish busy' are not captured (structure, handoff.json). A PATCH answered 200 {} leaves the hook's cache with profile undefined (useDraftSave setQueryData res.profile), so a state that must keep the recorded answers after a change answers the PATCH 500 instead (the save-failed line is then part of that state).",
  "overrides": {
    "onboarding-1": {
      "account": "M",
      "reach": "fixture",
      "why": "frame-1 is drawn for the returning member: M's recording has the drawn note, the knee limitation and five tabs. One edit opens the form on 5/5 (M's saved step is 0). M's recorded severity is 'avoid' (Kerülendő); the frame ticks 'caution' (Óvatosan) - the edit /profile/limitations/0/severity 'caution' is refused by pulse-fixture-check (no recording of GET /onboarding holds 'caution'), so the recorded value stays and the tick stands on the third row instead of the second (request R-S-onboarding-01).",
      "fixtures": [
        {
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/api/v1/onboarding",
          "edits": [
            {
              "pointer": "/profile/step",
              "value": 8
            }
